# Coding Conventions

- Pages `require_once __DIR__ . '/includes/bootstrap.php'` once.
- `htmlspecialchars()` every untrusted value shown as text. Exception: trusted
  catalog HTML in `descriptions_errors.php` `body` / `fix` on `help_errors.php`
  only — never echo request input as HTML.
- Prepared statements / bound parameters only. Table/column names in SQL come
  from `get_table_columns()` or fixed constants — never from request input.
- Validate run/group ids (`FILTER_VALIDATE_INT`) with an explicit 400 on failure.
- Prefer `array_filter` / `array_map` with `function ($x) { ... }` for column-list transforms, matching
  existing `render_helpers.php` style (PHP 5.4 — no arrow functions).
- Layout / classifier / column-order edits go in `includes/layouts/` — not inline
  in page files. No URLs in most layout files; the app owns hrefs. Exception:
  `layout_navbar.php` holds site-wide nav `href`s by design.
